      "attestations": [
        {
          "text": "WU Yen 吳炎 (T. 赤溟[民], H. 媿庵), d. July 1, 1663, age forty (sui), historian, was a native of Wu-chiang, Kiangsu. He and P'an Ch'êng-chang [q. v.] were co-authors of a history of the Ming dynasty and of a poetical account of that dynasty, the latter completed in 1656 under the title 今樂府 Chin yüeh-fu.",
